{"stream": "audit", "run_id": "res-ff3acbe0007e", "event": "outbound_call", "ts": 1787741353.048063, "service": "mcp", "endpoint": "http://localhost:8080/mcp", "method": "POST", "status": 200, "duration_ms": 2916.0, "attempt": 1, "error": "", "params": {"tool": "upsert_lead_profile", "employee_id": "E00019", "company_id": "C0019", "decision_maker_flag": "Yes", "lead_context": "Cedar is not just an observer of the AI-in-healthcare-billing trend — it is one of the most active builders in the space. Cedar's platform unifies billing, payments, coverage, and support into a single solution that continuously learns and adapts, powered by more than a billion patient interactions. The company is in the middle of an aggressive AI expansion: Cedar announced a major expansion of Cedar Intelligence, its AI-powered decision engine, with new capabilities embedded across its product suite, designed to help providers personalize billing journeys at scale, improve collections, and reduce cost-to-collect. On the agentic side, Cedar announced the Kora Platform in August 2026, evolving from a single AI billing agent to a suite of purpose-built AI agents that work together to recover patient revenue and reduce cost-to-collect. This push is directly tied to a macro pressure point Cedar is tracking closely: across Cedar's platform, nearly 40% of collectible dollars now come from patients without insurance coverage — up 54% in just three years — and the national hospital revenue impact due to the One Big Beautiful Bill Act could top $68.6 billion over 2026 and 2027. The broader industry is also crossing a threshold: revenue cycle management is emerging as one of the first areas where AI is delivering tangible, repeatable impact at scale. A post on running a successful AI pilot maps directly onto Cedar's current moment, as most providers will spend the next two years evaluating AI tools, running pilots, and adding to their vendor stack — and Cedar is both a vendor in that ecosystem and a company navigating its own internal AI rollouts. A strong opening question for a first conversation: *As Cedar scales Kora and Cedar Intelligence from pilot to production across its provider network, what has been the biggest internal challenge in moving from a successful AI proof-of-concept to consistent, measurable outcomes at scale?*"}}
